01:41:19,340 --> 01:41:20,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang maapektuhan ng El Nino.

1709
01:41:20,180 --> 01:41:23,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang mga mga apektuhan, individual yan, individual.

1710
01:41:25,660 --> 01:41:30,340
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero worst case scenario, baka 4.6 million.

1711
01:41:32,180 --> 01:41:36,100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 4.6 million, that's almost, tingin-tingin ako yung slides nyo kanina.

1712
01:41:36,740 --> 01:41:38,460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Halos lahat na yun, ha.

1713
01:41:39,800 --> 01:41:42,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi 6.7 million farmers, eh.

1714
01:41:45,120 --> 01:41:48,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yun yung worst case scenario namin, Mr. Chair.

1715
01:41:48,160 --> 01:41:49,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This is the worst case scenario.

1716
01:41:50,180 --> 01:42:02,540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So about 4 million out of the 9.6 million employment in the farming and fishery.

1717
01:42:02,540 --> 01:42:03,320
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 10.4, Mr. Chair.

1718
01:42:03,380 --> 01:42:05,740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nasa RSVSA lang.

1719
01:42:06,100 --> 01:42:06,980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So halos kalahati.

1720
01:42:07,920 --> 01:42:09,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yeah, halos kalahati, Mr. Chair.

1721
01:42:09,380 --> 01:42:10,120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Halos kalahati.

1722
01:42:10,700 --> 01:42:17,320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Looking at the budget, alam ko itong nag-uusap nga kami ni Chairman Kiko,

1723
01:42:17,320 --> 01:42:19,320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung presidential assistance.

1724
01:42:20,180 --> 01:42:21,760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To farmers and fisher folks.

1725
01:42:22,260 --> 01:42:25,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Of which, parang every year, nalalagay naman yun.

1726
01:42:25,280 --> 01:42:29,100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero ang nakakapagtaka sa NEP, hindi nalalagay ng budget.

1727
01:42:29,640 --> 01:42:31,320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ina-augment na lang ng Congress.

1728
01:42:31,480 --> 01:42:33,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Like last time, na-augment ng 10 billion.

1729
01:42:33,920 --> 01:42:38,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I understand, dito sa GAB, na-augment ulit, no?

1730
01:42:38,300 --> 01:42:39,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To 10 billion.

1731
01:42:39,620 --> 01:42:42,740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So aside from, itong 10 billion, I would assume,

1732
01:42:42,860 --> 01:42:47,060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: is also geared towards helping the 4 million farmers.

1733
01:42:47,240 --> 01:42:47,640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Tama po ba?

1734
01:42:47,720 --> 01:42:48,520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1735
01:42:48,520 --> 01:42:49,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And how do, how...

1736
01:42:50,180 --> 01:42:53,600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Paano makakatulong itong PAF, in presidential assistance,

1737
01:42:54,320 --> 01:42:59,760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: itong worst case scenario na 4 million farmers maapektuhan natin?

1738
01:42:59,860 --> 01:43:04,100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Well, Mr. Chair, yung presidential assistance to farmers and fisher folks,

1739
01:43:04,240 --> 01:43:09,420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: that is basically cash assistance, direct cash assistance to our farmers who are affected.

1740
01:43:10,640 --> 01:43:14,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Of course, sarami ngayon ang affected at 4.6 million.

1741
01:43:14,160 --> 01:43:15,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Medyo maliit yan.

1742
01:43:15,900 --> 01:43:19,460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But nag-uusap po kami sa kabinete.

1743
01:43:20,180 --> 01:43:24,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: With other, like Secretary of DOLE, Secretary of DSWD,

1744
01:43:25,080 --> 01:43:32,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na we're pooling now our funds para nga kung may tinamaan ng El Nino na hindi na talaga makatanim

1745
01:43:32,640 --> 01:43:35,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at walang trabaho.

1746
01:43:36,540 --> 01:43:41,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So may cash assistance, may food packs, may tupad,

1747
01:43:42,200 --> 01:43:45,420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: or maybe canal making or land preparation.

1748
01:43:45,420 --> 01:43:49,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So ganun ho ngayon yung diskarte namin.

1749
01:43:49,560 --> 01:43:54,000
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And moving forward to address para hindi yung dekahunt kaming lahat.

1750
01:43:54,440 --> 01:43:55,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So kung saan kailangan,

1751
01:43:56,220 --> 01:44:02,120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kagaya yung may El Nino sa Camarines Norte na may tinamaan na area na doon,

1752
01:44:03,000 --> 01:44:06,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na binanggit namin kay Sec. Rex Gachelian,

1753
01:44:07,020 --> 01:44:13,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: nagpadala ko kagad ng assistance ang DSWD in forms of cash din sa kanya dahil meron silang pondo.

1754
01:44:13,880 --> 01:44:17,840
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Kasi mas mabilis mag-respond at mag-replenish ang DSWD.

1755
01:44:18,080 --> 01:44:19,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So parang ganun na ho yung...

1756
01:44:19,560 --> 01:44:28,980
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: While 10 billion na PATH na ninalagay natin namin for 2027 sa direct cash assistance,

1757
01:44:29,520 --> 01:44:33,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: meron na kami access ngayon sa DSWD through them,

1758
01:44:34,080 --> 01:44:35,020
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: tsaka sa DOLI rin.

1759
01:44:35,440 --> 01:44:37,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So yun ho yung mas magandang sistema namin ngayon.

1760
01:44:38,980 --> 01:44:46,700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Later on, meron kaming ginawang special committee for economic recovery.

1761
01:44:46,700 --> 01:44:48,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we included, si Majority Leader Migs,

1762
01:44:49,560 --> 01:44:52,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: include niya na rin doon yung El Nino.

1763
01:44:52,800 --> 01:44:58,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So hingi kami ng detailed briefing on the government's response to El Nino.

1764
01:44:58,520 --> 01:44:59,840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi...

1765
01:44:59,840 --> 01:45:00,680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: padating na siya eh.

1766
01:45:00,760 --> 01:45:09,280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And it can be as worse as the Iran conflict in which yung presyo ng langis tumaas.

1767
01:45:09,740 --> 01:45:16,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ito naman, triple whammy. Wala ka ng trabaho, wala ka ng output, wala pa tayong makakain.

1768
01:45:16,800 --> 01:45:23,700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So we really need to make sure na ang gobyerno ay handa pagdating sa El Nino.

1769
01:45:23,700 --> 01:45:29,720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And so far, narinig ko kanina sa inyong briefing na meron na kayong parang whole of government approach.

1770
01:45:30,000 --> 01:45:34,800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To conserve resources between DOLE, DSWD, and DA.

1771
01:45:35,600 --> 01:45:40,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ganun ba ang approach, Secretary, to itong mga vulnerable sectors?

1772
01:45:40,480 --> 01:45:52,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair. Not only that, pati sa DOH, meron din tayong collaborative with DOLE, DOH, DSWD, and maybe other agencies pa.

1773
01:45:52,380 --> 01:45:59,960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: OCD pala, pati sa OCD under the DND.

1774
01:46:00,000 --> 01:46:09,060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Aside from PAF, what other components in the budget na gagamitin ninyo to respond to El Nino?

1775
01:46:09,400 --> 01:46:18,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron din tayo, Mr. Chair, fuel assistance, of course, some fertilizer support, seed support, and transport support, no?

1776
01:46:19,760 --> 01:46:29,340
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung logistic support na, like sa tollways, meron tayong mga agreement, and hopefully we can get more funding for that, among others, Mr. Chair.

1777
01:46:29,340 --> 01:46:29,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

1778
01:46:30,000 --> 01:46:33,460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's embedded already in the budget ng DA?

1779
01:46:33,460 --> 01:46:34,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1780
01:46:34,620 --> 01:46:35,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, thank you.

1781
01:46:36,200 --> 01:46:46,240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And on a detailed submission na lang, pakisubmit na lang, Secretary, yung DA's response to the El Nino.

1782
01:46:47,060 --> 01:46:47,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1783
01:46:47,900 --> 01:46:55,700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll jump to another topic, Secretary, and ito na pag-usapan natin last year, yung farm-to-market roads.

1784
01:46:55,980 --> 01:46:59,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And for 2026, yung farm-to-market roads.

1785
01:47:00,000 --> 01:47:15,940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung farm-to-market roads, nabigay, o tinransfer namin ni Senator Kiko, siya being the chairman of the budget of the DA, to the Department of Agriculture instead of the Department of Public Works.

1786
01:47:16,540 --> 01:47:24,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But nakita ko dito sa utilization for 2026, hindi pa siya nai-utilize to date.

1787
01:47:24,080 --> 01:47:28,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, may we get a briefing on...

1788
01:47:30,000 --> 01:47:43,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Tapos yung concept na yun, tinransfer natin sa DA, and then second, base dito sa aming report, doon sa 33 billion na farm-to-market roads, wala pang nagagawa for 2026.

1789
01:47:44,920 --> 01:47:51,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Before you answer, just to place on record, we'd like to acknowledge the presence of our minority leader, Senator Alan Cayetano.

1790
01:47:52,120 --> 01:47:52,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

1791
01:47:53,700 --> 01:47:54,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, please.

1792
01:47:54,900 --> 01:47:56,080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair.

1793
01:47:57,540 --> 01:47:58,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung sa FMR...

1794
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:11,080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: May transfer na ho sa amin yan, at may mga conditions under the GAAD for the transfer that we had to set up several offices, you know, get more people together.

1795
01:48:11,380 --> 01:48:13,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: May delay kami sa requesting of SARO.

1796
01:48:14,560 --> 01:48:20,080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But of course, na-request naman yung SARO namin, I think, by mid-year this year.

1797
01:48:20,840 --> 01:48:24,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But then, yung pera, dumating din lang September.

1798
01:48:24,820 --> 01:48:28,400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At then, nung binigay sa amin yung pera ng September,

1799
01:48:30,000 --> 01:48:34,140
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: it's an end of a quarter that we had to give it back, no?

1800
01:48:34,380 --> 01:48:35,460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung pondo.

1801
01:48:36,000 --> 01:48:39,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At inire-release lang ulit ngayon yung pondo sa amin this October.

1802
01:48:40,360 --> 01:48:46,100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But on the positive note naman, Mr. Chair, we're ready to bid now.

1803
01:48:47,420 --> 01:48:53,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At finally, matutuloy na ho yung implementation ng FMR natin for 2026.

1804
01:48:53,920 --> 01:48:57,960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And for 2027, pag na-approve na ho sa BICAM na yan,

1805
01:48:58,680 --> 01:48:59,840
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: we will be doing...

1806
01:49:00,000 --> 01:49:08,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pre-procurement basis sa NEP and short of award

1807
01:49:08,440 --> 01:49:14,580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: so that magmapabilis namin yung implementation yan sa 2027 also, Mr. Chair.

1808
01:49:14,940 --> 01:49:23,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Itong 33 billion na FMR, kaka-transfer lang sa inyo, kaka-release lang ng SARO itong September?

1809
01:49:24,640 --> 01:49:28,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Actually, ang na-release lang sa amin is 4.2 billion, Mr. Chair.

1810
01:49:28,160 --> 01:49:29,600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 4.2 billion.

1811
01:49:30,000 --> 01:49:30,640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So may...

1812
01:49:30,640 --> 01:49:32,680
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nung September.

1813
01:49:33,040 --> 01:49:37,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tapos binalik namin yan, we had to return it dahil may end of the month cut-off kami.

1814
01:49:38,420 --> 01:49:44,220
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Then binalik naman sa amin by this October lang yung 18 billion out of the 33, Mr. Chair.

1815
01:49:44,880 --> 01:49:45,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

1816
01:49:45,700 --> 01:49:48,580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So magkano na ang na-release for 2026 lang?

1817
01:49:49,040 --> 01:49:49,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 18...

1818
01:49:49,880 --> 01:49:52,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 23 billion na pala.

1819
01:49:52,460 --> 01:49:53,740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 23 billion. Okay.

1820
01:49:53,740 --> 01:49:59,980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And doon sa special provisions in which si Sen. Kiko ang nagsulat nun,

1821
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:08,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: may mga requirements, for example, yung transparency, ilalagay sa portal, ilalagay sa website.

1822
01:50:09,120 --> 01:50:11,880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ito ba ay naka-ayos na?

1823
01:50:12,260 --> 01:50:16,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, naka-setup na ho at ready to go.

1824
01:50:16,700 --> 01:50:24,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So now, the challenge, nandito na yung challenge namin na maayos to at nakita na lahat ng tao how we perform.

1825
01:50:24,600 --> 01:50:29,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And I have required actually our team sa DA to give a monthly report.

1826
01:50:29,920 --> 01:50:39,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: To me, on the status of each and every project with pictures, which I will also copy the committee chairman, Mr. Chair.

1827
01:50:39,460 --> 01:50:42,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, during the last hearing, it was a challenge to you.

1828
01:50:42,840 --> 01:50:46,980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil doon sa DPWH, iba-iba yung presyo.

1829
01:50:46,980 --> 01:50:58,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But I remember during that time, you said the DA can construct it more efficiently and much cheaper through the BAFE.

1830
01:50:59,280 --> 01:50:59,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ito ba ang BAFE?

1831
01:50:59,900 --> 01:51:05,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I, ano ba ito, na-increase ba yung capacity nila?

1832
01:51:05,800 --> 01:51:12,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi yun rin yung isang worry namin, baka mabulunan yung BAFE, DA BAFE.

1833
01:51:12,460 --> 01:51:15,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Have you already capacitated yung BAFE?

1834
01:51:15,400 --> 01:51:20,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Well, we have increased its capacity but not enough, Mr. Chair.

1835
01:51:20,620 --> 01:51:23,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But it will be a challenge.

1836
01:51:24,260 --> 01:51:28,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: It's not, hindi ito magiging madali but we will do our best.

1837
01:51:28,780 --> 01:51:42,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: We assigned a special undersecretary just to look into all of this team para may nakatutok na 100% so that we do it properly.

1838
01:51:43,480 --> 01:51:48,340
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung sa presyo naman, at that time, we can make it lower.

1839
01:51:48,340 --> 01:51:58,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: As of now, bumalik kami sa original considering naman na prices of everything has gone.

1840
01:51:58,780 --> 01:51:59,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Much, much higher.

1841
01:52:00,420 --> 01:52:06,640
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But we were able to maintain yung dating presyo at 15 million per kilometer

1842
01:52:06,640 --> 01:52:10,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: which even yung contractor, sinasabi, medyo maliit na yung margin nila

1843
01:52:10,900 --> 01:52:19,700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: but payag naman na kailangan lahat ng trabaho at kailangan ng projects naman ng mga contractors.

1844
01:52:19,700 --> 01:52:28,620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So for normal, on a normal condition, 15 million per kilometer pa ba ang cost?

1845
01:52:28,620 --> 01:52:30,380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nang farm-to-market roads?

1846
01:52:30,600 --> 01:52:32,460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa ngayon, yun ang tamang cost na yun.

1847
01:52:32,500 --> 01:52:33,420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yun ang tamang cost.

1848
01:52:33,600 --> 01:52:39,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Of course, as you inspected, may iba nasa Bangil, di ba?

1849
01:52:39,880 --> 01:52:43,100
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But on the average, assuming all things equal, 15 million ang cost.

1850
01:52:43,100 --> 01:52:44,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yan yung average, Mr. Chair.

1851
01:52:44,620 --> 01:52:45,220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yan ang average.

1852
01:52:45,700 --> 01:52:47,240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

1853
01:52:47,440 --> 01:52:51,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll just ask some more questions on my second round.

1854
01:52:51,380 --> 01:52:52,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, thank you.

1855
01:52:54,060 --> 01:52:57,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Senator JV, Chairman of the Committee,

1856
01:52:58,620 --> 01:52:59,560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: please, you have the floor.

1857
01:53:01,080 --> 01:53:02,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1858
01:53:02,880 --> 01:53:06,020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Good morning to Secretary Laurel, the DA family.

1859
01:53:07,240 --> 01:53:10,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This was asked earlier, no, ng ating po, Senate President,

1860
01:53:10,240 --> 01:53:17,380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung tungkol po sa Presidential Assistance to Farmers and Fisher Folk Program,

1861
01:53:17,380 --> 01:53:19,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: being the Chair of the Committee on Finance,

1862
01:53:19,280 --> 01:53:23,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I noticed, as pointed out by our Senate President,

1863
01:53:23,340 --> 01:53:28,080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: wala po ito sa NEP, but it was included in the House,

1864
01:53:28,620 --> 01:53:31,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: HGAB, or General Appropriations Bill from the House,

1865
01:53:31,940 --> 01:53:32,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: sa 10 billion.

1866
01:53:33,540 --> 01:53:40,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just want to ask, did the agency request it for this?

1867
01:53:40,780 --> 01:53:43,620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: O ang house ang naglagay nito?

1868
01:53:45,020 --> 01:53:45,620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes.

1869
