4925
04:45:47,340 --> 04:45:54,760
DA Undersecretary for Inspectorate and Enforcement Carlos C. Carag: And then we can certify some rendering facilities in areas where we have major seaports.

4926
04:45:55,440 --> 04:45:56,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, okay.

4927
04:45:56,820 --> 04:46:05,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we will continue to monitor that until finally we will have your facilities necessary to do your job.

4928
04:46:07,420 --> 04:46:19,300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The other concern that I raised in the onion smuggling, onion heating in Nueva Ecija was the,

4929
04:46:20,580 --> 04:46:22,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and this is my last point before I turn over.

4930
04:46:22,480 --> 04:46:25,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's the...

4931
04:46:26,820 --> 04:46:34,960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Memorandum of Agreement that I asked the DA to sign with the PSA.

4932
04:46:35,760 --> 04:46:45,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The reason being that in that hearing in Nueva Ecija on the onions, the over-importation of onions,

4933
04:46:45,400 --> 04:46:54,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: it was established that the PSA data is different from the Bureau of Plant Data.

4934
04:46:55,680 --> 04:46:56,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Lumalabas sa BP.

4935
04:46:56,820 --> 04:47:10,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kulang ng 62,000 metric tons yung kanilang data in terms of production.

4936
04:47:12,100 --> 04:47:16,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mas marami ng 62,000 metric tons ang PSA.

4937
04:47:17,500 --> 04:47:25,320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, dahil dun, kulang ang supply according to DA, kaya nag-import.

4938
04:47:25,320 --> 04:47:26,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Naglabas ng...

4939
04:47:26,820 --> 04:47:30,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang SPC, para makapasok itong onions.

4940
04:47:30,260 --> 04:47:39,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang problema, pumasok ng after or during harvest season na, for some reason.

4941
04:47:40,500 --> 04:47:48,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, to fix that problem, I asked, and that a memorandum of agreement be entered into, right?

4942
04:47:48,700 --> 04:47:49,380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And this is it.

4943
04:47:50,540 --> 04:47:53,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang problema nyo rito, hindi pa pirmado si...

4944
04:47:53,220 --> 04:47:55,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yusek Bayate.

4945
04:47:55,540 --> 04:47:56,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ma'am, hindi pa kayo pumipirmado.

4946
04:47:56,820 --> 04:47:57,060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi pa kayo pumipirma.

4947
04:47:58,740 --> 04:47:59,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Wala rito eh.

4948
04:48:01,320 --> 04:48:02,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Baka...

4949
04:48:02,080 --> 04:48:06,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At yung National Corn, nasaan si Program Director Wagas?

4950
04:48:07,460 --> 04:48:14,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sabi ko kasi sa inyo, yung budget ninyo ay nakasalalay dito sa pag-draft nito.

4951
04:48:15,820 --> 04:48:22,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Eh, yan yung beauty ng check and balance, di ba, na ginagawa natin.

4952
04:48:22,100 --> 04:48:26,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, kung maaaring pirmahan ninyo bago mag-plenary para kompleto na ito,

4953
04:48:26,820 --> 04:48:27,820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: no?

4954
04:48:28,300 --> 04:48:31,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pati si Mr. Wagas, andito ba yung project director?

4955
04:48:32,780 --> 04:48:34,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, pirmahan na ninyo.

4956
04:48:35,440 --> 04:48:38,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nauna na magpumirma si Secretary Kiko eh.

4957
04:48:38,800 --> 04:48:38,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ha?

4958
04:48:39,400 --> 04:48:41,380
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Hindi dumating sa office ko, ano eh.

4959
04:48:44,180 --> 04:48:45,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat may group chat kayo.

4960
04:48:48,820 --> 04:48:50,760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But anyway, please, no?

4961
04:48:51,760 --> 04:48:52,760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If...

4962
04:48:52,760 --> 04:48:54,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Again, before plenary, ha?

4963
04:48:56,820 --> 04:48:58,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And then...

4964
04:48:58,700 --> 04:49:05,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We can now...

4965
04:49:05,800 --> 04:49:08,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, so, nasaan si Mr. Wagas?

4966
04:49:09,800 --> 04:49:10,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, hindi.

4967
04:49:11,300 --> 04:49:13,380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pakisagot na lang, napipirmahan ninyo, tama?

4968
04:49:14,660 --> 04:49:16,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Para magkaroon ng...

4969
04:49:16,040 --> 04:49:23,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Para ang PSA data at ang DA data on our production, iisa.

4970
04:49:23,640 --> 04:49:26,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi yung mas marami yung...

4971
04:49:26,820 --> 04:49:36,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya, dahil kulang mag-import.

4972
04:49:36,800 --> 04:49:37,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

4973
04:49:39,800 --> 04:49:41,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, where is Mr. Wagas?

4974
04:49:41,600 --> 04:49:41,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

4975
04:49:43,860 --> 04:49:47,940
DA National Corn Program Director Abel F. Wagas: Your Honor, sir, pipirmahan po namin.

4976
04:49:48,160 --> 04:49:48,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, thank you.

4977
04:49:49,020 --> 04:49:50,420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yun lang ang kailangan ko marinig sa inyo.

4978
04:49:51,460 --> 04:49:55,060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: USEC, Bayate, sabi nyo na, pirmahan na ninyo.

4979
04:49:56,180 --> 04:49:56,800
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: It's set.

4980
04:49:56,800 --> 04:50:00,460
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: It only stayed in my office for one day.

4981
04:50:00,560 --> 04:50:01,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ba't hindi pa nakapirma rito?

4982
04:50:02,120 --> 04:50:02,800
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: I don't know.

4983
04:50:03,080 --> 04:50:05,980
DA Undersecretary Drusila Esther E. Bayate: Basta, I make it a point na ganyan po yung senator.

4984
04:50:06,300 --> 04:50:08,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, if you've signed it, thank you.

4985
04:50:08,900 --> 04:50:10,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ito lang ang binigay ng PSA sa amin.

4986
04:50:11,760 --> 04:50:16,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But since you've signed it and he will sign it, Mr. Wagas will sign it.

4987
04:50:16,680 --> 04:50:17,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we're good.

4988
04:50:19,200 --> 04:50:20,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we're good.

4989
04:50:20,640 --> 04:50:22,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Secretary, for this.

4990
04:50:22,400 --> 04:50:26,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, we can ensure that the data is rationalized.

4991
04:50:26,800 --> 04:50:31,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The information is iisa.

4992
04:50:31,820 --> 04:50:37,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang hirap nung dalawang iisa gobyerno, dalawa datos, di ba?

4993
04:50:38,600 --> 04:50:40,320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: On the matter of supply.

4994
04:50:40,860 --> 04:50:41,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Huwag naman, di ba?

4995
04:50:42,740 --> 04:50:44,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Para ma-reconcile natin.

4996
04:50:44,680 --> 04:50:44,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

4997
04:50:45,440 --> 04:50:48,300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we thank the good Secretary for this.

4998
04:50:49,440 --> 04:50:53,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And now, I turn the floor to the next round of Senator Aimee.

4999
04:50:53,580 --> 04:50:54,380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ma'am, you have the floor.

5000
04:50:54,480 --> 04:50:54,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead.

5001
04:50:54,800 --> 04:50:55,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You have 10 minutes.

5002
04:50:55,600 --> 04:50:56,120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Chair.

5003
04:50:56,120 --> 04:50:56,760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Or even more.

5004
04:50:56,840 --> 04:50:58,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because you're the only one left.

5005
04:50:59,660 --> 04:51:00,960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mag-duduwet tayo.

5006
04:51:01,220 --> 04:51:01,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Go ahead.

5007
04:51:01,400 --> 04:51:05,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ako maraming salamat, Mr. Chair at Senator Kiko.

5008
04:51:05,780 --> 04:51:08,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Following up dun sa tanong ninyo tungkol sa sibuyas,

5009
04:51:08,640 --> 04:51:15,980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: magtatanong nang ako dito sa pinakasikat sa onion and garlic, yung Lea Cruz.

5010
04:51:16,620 --> 04:51:18,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Balibalita, namamayagpag na ulit.

5011
04:51:18,980 --> 04:51:25,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Samantalang meron siyang record-breaking fine ng 1.76 billion na administrative

5012
04:51:25,640 --> 04:51:26,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: dyan sa...

5013
04:51:26,800 --> 04:51:29,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: competition, commission, ano?

5014
04:51:30,220 --> 04:51:30,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Paano ba yun?

5015
04:51:31,060 --> 04:51:36,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos, maliban dyan, dapat may criminal charges pa rin at sandigan ba yan?

5016
04:51:37,000 --> 04:51:40,420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero sa kabila ng lahat na yan, mga kaso-kasong yan,

5017
04:51:41,400 --> 04:51:46,240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: mainit ang balita na andyan na naman siya sa sibuyas at bawang.

5018
04:51:46,740 --> 04:51:53,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano po ang update natin tungkol sa Lea Cruz at yung mga grupo ng allium na yan?

5019
04:51:53,880 --> 04:51:56,520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: First of all, Mr. Chair, hindi ko kilala yan.

5020
04:51:56,520 --> 04:52:04,120
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Si Lea Cruz, narinig ko lang din sa dyaryo nung isang araw and I'm surprised na sa hatol sa kanya

5021
04:52:04,120 --> 04:52:09,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: and happy in a sense dahil nga at least justice will be served.

5022
04:52:09,440 --> 04:52:15,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Well, very happy po kami kasi sa onion and garlic producers, notorious po ito.

5023
04:52:15,940 --> 04:52:19,140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kaya nga lang narinig namin na nangangalakal pa rin.

5024
04:52:19,940 --> 04:52:26,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So ngayon, Mr. Chair, as far as red onion is concerned, wala tayong importasyon ng red onion.

5025
04:52:26,520 --> 04:52:30,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: For this year and hopefully, baka next year, halos wala rin.

5026
04:52:30,760 --> 04:52:32,520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa puti at sa bawang.

5027
04:52:32,520 --> 04:52:40,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa puti, ngayon lang tayo nag-umpisa ng white onion importasyon and very limited quantity lang ho yan.

5028
04:52:41,140 --> 04:52:45,300
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: It is distributed equally among the most people who applied.

5029
04:52:46,100 --> 04:52:52,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And I have not heard of Lea Cruz.

5030
04:52:53,280 --> 04:52:56,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But kung yan ho ang impormasyon nyo, I will investigate.

5031
04:52:56,520 --> 04:52:58,700
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: I will investigate and deeper ang nakikinig naman yung enforcement natin.

5032
04:52:58,700 --> 04:53:06,140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Papatulong lang po kami sa DA na pursigihin hindi lang yung napakalaking fine na pinapalakpakang po namin,

5033
04:53:06,220 --> 04:53:15,680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na 1.76 billion, kundi pati na rin yung criminal charges na dapat pursigihin sa DOJ at sa Sandigan.

5034
04:53:16,220 --> 04:53:25,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ah, yes. Sige ho. I will try to pursue it with Secretary Vida and the others para nga mahuli ka agad at magbayad siya ka agad.

5035
04:53:25,540 --> 04:53:26,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you very much.

5036
04:53:26,520 --> 04:53:28,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you very much po. Malit lang yan sa kanya.

5037
04:53:28,820 --> 04:53:40,660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ngayon sa post-harvest, sangayon po kami sa sinasabi ninyo na yung NIA sana tumutok doon sa big ticket items like the dams, the impoundment and so on.

5038
04:53:41,020 --> 04:53:44,480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sangayon rin kami doon sa post-harvest na sinasabi po ninyo.

5039
04:53:44,920 --> 04:53:48,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero ang kasabihan, put your money where your mouth is.

5040
04:53:48,300 --> 04:53:56,500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pag tinignan yung budget ng DA, hindi maliwanag kung saan yung post-harvest ang tanging nanging ibabaw.

5041
04:53:56,520 --> 04:54:02,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh yung figure na napakaliit na nasa BIFAR, 516 million lamang.

5042
04:54:02,800 --> 04:54:13,580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero nabanggit ninyo na nagkakaroon na tayo ng mga cold storage na magaganda, katulad sa tagig, tapos may logistics chain, may mga distribution and marketing effort.

5043
04:54:14,660 --> 04:54:19,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Magkano ba talaga ang ginagastos ng DA para sa post-harvest? Para sa kaalaman lang namin.

5044
04:54:23,900 --> 04:54:24,420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ah...

5045
04:54:24,420 --> 04:54:26,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi meron rin banggit dito na...

5046
04:54:26,520 --> 04:54:30,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Naulit yata ni Secretary yung mechanical dryer, 380 pieces.

5047
04:54:31,540 --> 04:54:35,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At natuwa naman kami no, nabalitaan namin sa diaryo.

5048
04:54:39,480 --> 04:54:43,960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Apakaliit eh, parang hindi siya priority pag tinignan yung budget.

5049
04:54:43,960 --> 04:54:50,460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ah yung sa, ah Mr. Chair, yung sa post-harvest natin, may 4.5 billion ano?

5050
04:54:51,360 --> 04:54:53,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi pa kasama yun sa RCEF o how much?

5051
04:54:53,620 --> 04:54:56,240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Where is the 4.5 billion?

5052
04:54:56,520 --> 04:54:59,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Located po? Under what category?

5053
04:54:59,960 --> 04:55:02,840
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa mga banner programs po yan, Mr. Chair.

5054
04:55:02,960 --> 04:55:03,260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa alin?

5055
04:55:03,300 --> 04:55:07,580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Kalat-kalat sa banner programs like National Rice Program, Coconut.

5056
04:55:08,180 --> 04:55:11,200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: May RCEF, may National Rice Program.

5057
04:55:11,880 --> 04:55:13,860
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Corn Program, Madam Chair.

5058
04:55:14,380 --> 04:55:24,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, may we inquire lamang kung maari, bigyan lang kami ng listahan para maipakita na tinututukan naman yung post-harvest dahil yun nga ang daing ng napakarami.

5059
04:55:24,740 --> 04:55:25,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 23% na...

5060
04:55:26,520 --> 04:55:34,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ngayon, medyo mas maganda ang numero, sinasabing 16 to 17, pero parang hindi pa rin ramdam, ano?

5061
04:55:34,300 --> 04:55:38,320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang laki nun kung tutuusin para sa problema natin sa bigas.

5062
04:55:38,480 --> 04:55:41,000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, we're really keen on following that up.

5063
04:55:41,500 --> 04:55:45,960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair, we will supply all the data and kung anong ginagawa.

5064
04:55:46,200 --> 04:55:51,840
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: But sa totoo lang, kulang din ang pondo. We need more post-harvest facilities, Mr. Chair.

5065
04:55:51,840 --> 04:55:55,960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, I only had a question.

5066
04:55:56,520 --> 04:56:00,780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I also had a question with regard to NTA, yung tobacco.

5067
04:56:01,680 --> 04:56:12,760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The tobacco fund had 11... had 116 billion at the end of 2025 with the projected collections of 13 billion.

5068
04:56:13,420 --> 04:56:19,340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And yet, its proposed expenditure is only 699 million.

5069
04:56:19,840 --> 04:56:20,600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Napakaliit.

5070
04:56:20,600 --> 04:56:24,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kung tutuusin, ihahambing mo sa billion-billion na kinikita.

5071
04:56:25,640 --> 04:56:26,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Eh...

5072
04:56:26,360 --> 04:56:32,020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How much of that reported balance is actually available and legally usable?

5073
04:56:32,440 --> 04:56:37,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And what prevents a larger allocation for eligible tobacco farmer assistance?

5074
04:56:37,940 --> 04:56:41,200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit napapako sa wala pang 700 million?

5075
04:56:42,960 --> 04:56:44,280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nagtataka lang ako.

5076
04:56:44,800 --> 04:56:50,180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung allocation sa budget ninyo, 143 million.

5077
04:56:50,660 --> 04:56:53,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Personal services, ganon din.

5078
04:56:54,040 --> 04:56:55,880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: 143 million halos.

5079
04:56:56,360 --> 04:57:01,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, ibig sabihin, ang farmer assistance na ibibigay, eh nasa 200 million na lang.

5080
04:57:03,440 --> 04:57:04,380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nakakatawa po eh.

5081
04:57:04,480 --> 04:57:13,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why is the entire net increase in the NTA budget to be dedicated solely to higher personnel costs?

5082
04:57:13,880 --> 04:57:19,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Magtataas ba silang lahat ng sweldo rather than expansion of direct farmer assistance?

5083
04:57:19,840 --> 04:57:21,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, that's two questions.

5084
04:57:21,320 --> 04:57:26,320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How much money talaga yung NTA samantalang laki-laki ng levy?

5085
04:57:26,360 --> 04:57:32,340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At ikalawa, bakit naman puro personal na lang ang bibigyan at hindi yung mismong farmer?

5086
04:57:33,120 --> 04:57:37,060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Madam, Mr. Chair, we'll ask NTA head to explain.

5087
04:57:40,000 --> 04:57:41,500
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Good afternoon po, Madam Chair.

5088
04:57:41,620 --> 04:57:44,640
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Yung increase po na binigay is for...

5089
04:57:44,640 --> 04:57:50,000
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Sa PS po napuntayin, dun po sa nung in-implement yung CPCS2.

5090
04:57:50,600 --> 04:57:53,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano yun? Sorry, sorry. Naa-alpha-benzupa ko.

5091
04:57:53,360 --> 04:57:54,360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa...

5092
04:57:54,360 --> 04:57:55,360
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Sa...

5093
04:57:56,360 --> 04:58:04,260
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Nung in-implement po yung CPCS2, yung conference, ano?

5094
04:58:06,600 --> 04:58:12,240
NTA Administrator and CEO Belinda Sarmiento-Sanchez: Increase ng sahod po across the board ng lahat ng government agencies, mga DOCC po.

